---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SeaBreak from '../../components/SeaBreak.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import { celestial, scenes } from '../../config/images';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'Elements & Modalities', href: '/explore/elements-and-modalities/' },
];

const zodiacGrid = [
  { element: 'Fire', cardinal: 'Aries', fixed: 'Leo', mutable: 'Sagittarius' },
  { element: 'Earth', cardinal: 'Capricorn', fixed: 'Taurus', mutable: 'Virgo' },
  { element: 'Air', cardinal: 'Libra', fixed: 'Aquarius', mutable: 'Gemini' },
  { element: 'Water', cardinal: 'Cancer', fixed: 'Scorpio', mutable: 'Pisces' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Elements and Modalities: the two grids behind the zodiac"
  description="Fire, earth, air, and water crossed with cardinal, fixed, and mutable create the twelve signs. Learn the system beneath the zodiac rather than memorizing twelve disconnected personalities."
  path="/explore/elements-and-modalities/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
        <h1>Elements and modalities</h1>
        <p class="lede">The twelve signs make much more sense when you see the system underneath them. Four elements crossed with three modalities produce twelve distinct combinations, one for each sign.</p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img"
        src={scenes.signs.src}
        srcset={scenes.signs.srcset}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt={scenes.signs.alt}
        width={scenes.signs.width}
        height={scenes.signs.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose flow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
        <p class="eyebrow">See the system first</p>
        <h2>Four elements × three modalities = twelve signs</h2>
        <p>Each sign occupies one unique coordinate. Read across for modality; read down for element.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="zodiac-matrix" role="table" aria-label="Elements and modalities of the twelve zodiac signs">
        <div class="matrix-head" role="row">
          <span role="columnheader">Element</span><span role="columnheader">Cardinal · begins</span><span role="columnheader">Fixed · sustains</span><span role="columnheader">Mutable · adapts</span>
        </div>
        {zodiacGrid.map((row) => (
          <div class="matrix-row" role="row">
            <strong role="rowheader">{row.element}</strong>
            <span role="cell">{row.cardinal}</span>
            <span role="cell">{row.fixed}</span>
            <span role="cell">{row.mutable}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="card__meta" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">The grid is a teaching structure, not a personality scorecard. A full chart gives each combination context.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Two coordinates, twelve combinations</h2>
      <p>
        Each sign belongs to one <em>element</em> and one <em>modality</em>. No two signs share the
        same combination. Aries is cardinal fire, Taurus fixed earth, Gemini mutable air, and so on.
        This structure is one of the reasons I prefer teaching the zodiac as a system instead of as
        twelve separate lists of personality traits.
      </p>

      <h2>The four elements</h2>
      <p>Elements describe broad modes of engagement and emphasis.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fire</strong> (Aries, Leo, Sagittarius): animation, initiative, confidence, enthusiasm, and the impulse to move toward experience.</li>
        <li><strong>Earth</strong> (Taurus, Virgo, Capricorn): material reality, practicality, embodiment, maintenance, and attention to what can be made useful or durable.</li>
        <li><strong>Air</strong> (Gemini, Libra, Aquarius): thought, exchange, comparison, language, relationship among ideas, and the ability to gain perspective.</li>
        <li><strong>Water</strong> (Cancer, Scorpio, Pisces): feeling, receptivity, attachment, intuition, memory, and sensitivity to what is happening beneath the surface.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These are symbolic categories, not personality verdicts. A chart with strong fire does not
        automatically describe an impulsive person, and a chart with less earth does not prove
        someone is impractical. Planets, houses, aspects, rulerships, and lived experience all add
        context.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SeaBreak image={celestial.seedlings} />

  <section class="section section--sea">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>The three modalities</h2>
      <p>Modalities describe how a sign tends to move through a process. They also correspond to a sign's position within a season.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cardinal</strong> (Aries, Cancer, Libra, Capricorn): initiating, directing, beginning, and setting something in motion.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed</strong> (Taurus, Leo, Scorpio, Aquarius): sustaining, stabilizing, concentrating, deepening, and holding a course.</li>
        <li><strong>Mutable</strong> (Gemini, Virgo, Sagittarius, Pisces): adapting, distributing, translating, changing form, and preparing for transition.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Signs sharing a modality form squares and oppositions to one another around the zodiac. That
        geometric relationship is part of why they may describe different ways of approaching the
        same kind of task: cardinal signs all initiate, for example, but they do so through four very
        different elements.
      </p>

      <h2>Putting the grids together</h2>
      <p>
        This is where the system becomes memorable. Scorpio is fixed water: water's emotional depth
        operating through fixed concentration. Gemini is mutable air: air's exchange of ideas moving
        through adaptation. Capricorn is cardinal earth: material reality approached through
        initiation and direction.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also look at elemental and modal emphasis across a whole chart, but I would resist
        turning the count into a diagnosis. A pattern becomes meaningful when we ask which planets
        are carrying that emphasis, where they are placed, and how the person actually lives it.
        Structure first; synthesis next.
      </p>
      <p>Next: <a href="/explore/signs/">the twelve signs one by one</a>, or <a href="/explore/aspects/">how aspects work</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Ready to use the grid?"
    body="The signs show each element-and-modality combination in practice. Aspects show how those sign relationships also become geometry inside a chart."
    buttonLabel="Explore the Signs"
    buttonHref="/explore/signs/"
    secondaryLabel="Learn the Aspects"
    secondaryHref="/explore/aspects/"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .zodiac-matrix { display: grid; gap: 1px; background: var(--color-border); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); overflow: hidden; }
  .matrix-head, .matrix-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(6rem,.7fr) repeat(3,1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--color-border); }
  .matrix-head > *, .matrix-row > * { background: var(--color-surface); padding: var(--space-4); }
  .matrix-head > * { font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 700; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .zodiac-matrix { background: transparent; border: 0; gap: var(--space-4); overflow: visible; }
    .matrix-head { display: none; }
    .matrix-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); overflow: hidden; background: transparent; }
    .matrix-row strong { background: var(--color-surface); }
    .matrix-row span::before { display: block; font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
    .matrix-row span:nth-child(2)::before { content: 'Cardinal · begins'; }
    .matrix-row span:nth-child(3)::before { content: 'Fixed · sustains'; }
    .matrix-row span:nth-child(4)::before { content: 'Mutable · adapts'; }
  }
</style>